  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Slot</strong> none; <strong>Price</strong> 5,000 gp (lesser), 10,000 gp (normal), 20,000 gp (greater)<br>\n<strong>Weight</strong> 5 lbs.; <strong>Feat Cost</strong> 1 sp</p>\n<p>Targets affected by a disruptive spell must attempt concentration checks when using talents or sphere-like abilities (DC equals the save DC of the disruptive spell plus 1/2 the caster level of the talent being cast (minimum 1)) for 1 round. Targets that avoid the talent’s effects avoid the effect of this feat or apparatus as well.</p>\n<p><strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nCraft Apparatus, Disruptive Spell; <strong>Cost</strong> 2,500 gp (lesser), 5,000 gp (normal), 10,000 gp (greater)</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/apparatuses-metamagic#toc18\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": "<p>Selected profile: lesser tier; held slender rod. Use as part of casting a qualifying sphere effect while holding this apparatus in at least one hand. Spend one of its three daily uses; only one metamagic apparatus may apply per casting. The apparatus does not require knowing its feat or paying that feat’s extra spell points/casting time. Normal sphere-effect costs and other known metamagic costs still apply. The chosen sphere effect must be caster level 7 or lower.</p><p>Only targets actually affected need concentration checks for one round. Use the disruptive effect’s save DC plus half the caster level of the talent being cast, minimum one; avoid an actor-wide concentration penalty.</p><p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/apparatuses-metamagic\">Shared metamagic apparatus rules</a>. The Feat Cost in the source applies to taking the feat instead of using the physical item.</p>",
      "unidentified": ""
    },
